# renki-config

A tool's configuration, as contracts. A setting has a kind, a scope and a
default, all in its type; a store is a file format that parses a document,
answers a key and writes one back; the resolver reads every declared setting
from five places in a fixed order and says which one won. Nothing here reads a
file or the environment, allocates, or names `std`: the launcher does that
and implements the store. `#![no_std]`, no alloc, notko for fallibility.
